# Motor spin thresholds, MEASURED on this airframe -- not defaults.
#
# Measured 2026-10-03 with props off, ESCs calibrated, pack at ~11.0 V:
#
#   1100 us  no motor starts
#   1150 us  no motor starts
#   1210 us  no motor starts
#   1250 us  ALL FOUR start
#
# So the ESCs' start threshold sits between 1210 and 1250 us, and all four
# are matched -- which is what makes it safe. The original symptom (one motor
# idle, another stopping as pitch/roll moved) was the stock MOT_SPIN_ARM 0.10
# = 1100 us sitting BELOW every threshold, with stabilisation pushing one
# output across at a time.
#
# On a 1000-2000 range: 1250 us = 0.25. ARM is set just above the measured
# start point, MIN a little above that, per ArduPilot's procedure.
#
# THESE ARE HIGH. A calibrated ESC usually starts near 1050-1100. Two things
# worth re-checking before accepting them permanently:
#   * the pack was at 3.66 V/cell when measured. A depleted battery gives
#     less torque, so motors need more throttle to break away -- re-measure
#     on a full pack and these may come down.
#   * MOT_THST_HOVER defaults to 0.35 and is learned in flight. If hover ends
#     up close to MOT_SPIN_MIN 0.30 there is very little room left to REDUCE
#     a motor for stabilisation, which shows up as sloppy or twitchy control.
#     If that happens, the answer is better-matched ESCs, not more trim.
MOT_SPIN_ARM,0.26
MOT_SPIN_MIN,0.30
